      "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/57b2e6/{size}.png",
      "created_at": "2012-08-20T16:17:13.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>I'm having a little trouble understanding how Unity's Cryo Bot card works given some of the rules clarifications that have been collected in Spiff's PDF.</p><p>Cryo Bot says: \"Whenever this card is dealt damage, it deals each none-hero target 1 cold damage.\" Cryo Bot has 1 HP.</p><p>Given the clarification that damage dealt = HP were reduced, meaning that HP must drop in order for damage to have been dealt, and the clarification that states if a card is destroyed any remaining effects of that card are immediately canceled, how is it possible for Cryo Bot to ever deal any damage? If it is dealt damage, it's destroyed because it only has 1 HP, and the remaining effect of it dealing damage is canceled.</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:36:02.679Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 6,
